SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause (pour's licence)

What joe's installer needs from pour that upstream (commit 02fb3a9) does
not have yet; the same changes, one commit each, are to be offered upstream:

- --target DIR: accounts, groups and homes go into another root (the disk
  being installed), through shadow's --prefix;
- password hashes are carried from the source's etc/shadow (chpasswd -e,
  on standard input); locked and empty ones are not;
- homes are accepted only as /home/<name>, and never written through a
  symbolic link;
- copied files lose set-uid and set-gid, entries owned by others are given
  to the account, and the copy is made under umask 077;
- an account whose name, uid or gid is taken in the target is skipped and
  reported, instead of ending the run;
- rpm databases are recognised and reported as unreadable, instead of
  silently finding nothing;
- the package map names joe's recipes;
- --json: one event per line, for the installer.

